<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia Jan palm oil output down 10.6 pct -MOPGC.</title>
<headline>Malaysia Jan palm oil output down 10.6 pct -MOPGC.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Malaysian Oil Palm Growers' Council (MOPGC) has estimated Malaysia's crude palm oil output in January at 570,000 tonnes, down 10.6 percent from December, traders who obtained the data said on Monday.</p>
<p>Private crop forecaster Ivan Wong had estimated January production at 578,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>The Palm Oil Registration and Licensing Authority is due to release official January crop data on February 22.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-8911)</p>
